NOTE for mesa (Iris Driver)

    If your system has a modern Intel GPU (any ASUS Zenbook, MacBook, or recent 
    laptop), you have i965-class hardware, not i915.
    Compiling only the i915 driver will result in AIGLX errors when X tries to
    load the graphics renderer.

    Read xorg/mesa/README.md for additional notes.

IMPORTANT

    You also need contrib/libva-intel-driver installed.
    This package provides the i965_drv_video.so video acceleration driver, which
    works alongside the Mesa i965 DRI driver for complete GPU support.


    Also you need

sudo mkdir -p /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d
sudo tee /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/20-intel.conf > /dev/null << 'EOF'
Section "Device"
    Identifier "Intel Graphics"
    Driver "modesetting"
    Option "AccelMethod" "glamor"
    Option "DRI" "3"
EndSection

Section "Module"
    Load "glx"
EndSection
EOF
